1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
Come to China's last Shangri-La a week too late — the gold is gone.
I'm your China Travel Expert

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:05,200
Daocheng Yading, deep in western Sichuan.

3
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:07,800
Its golden larch forests peak for about two weeks, late October.

4
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:10,000
Miss that window and the valleys turn bare and brown.

5
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:12,600
And you're high — the shuttle drops you near 3,900 metres.

6
00:00:12,600 --> 00:00:15,000
No private cars; park shuttles only to the trailheads.

7
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:17,200
Nights swing from 5 degrees to below freezing.

8
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:19,800
Double-tap if you'd plan a whole trip around two weeks of gold.

9
00:00:19,800 --> 00:00:23,000
★ Expert Tip: aim for the last week of October, and sleep a night in Daocheng to acclimatise.

10
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:25,800
Risk the altitude for the gold, or skip it? Tell me.
